<title>USA: Intermet Q4 boosted by tax benefits.</title>
<headline>Intermet Q4 boosted by tax benefits.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intermet Corp, posting higher fourth quarter earnings, said its continued profitability required recognition of almost $11 million in tax benefits previously reserved as deferred tax assets.</p>
<p>The manufacturer of precision iron and aluminum castings reported quarterly earnings of $16.7 million or $0.65 a share, up from $6 million or $0.24 a share.</p>
<p>Looking ahead, chairman John Doddridge said, &quot;Acquisitions made in the fourth quarter of 1996 will contribute to substantially improving the company's performance.&quot;</p>
<p>	 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
